{"baseRefName":"beta","body":"Closes #1019\n\n## (a) Numeric-id evidence\n\nZabbix item ids are constrained with `['required','string','max:32','regex:/^\\d+$/']` (Traffic) and `['required','string','max:64','regex:/^\\d+$/']` on `item_ids.*` (MultiLatest). Both controllers validate **before** any cache, lock, or upstream access — an arbitrary string can no longer mint a fresh cache key that forces an upstream call.\n\nEvidence for the numeric constraint: across all five id columns of `zabbix_devices`, the non-numeric count is **0 over 39 rows** (`item_id`, `out_item_id`, `in_item_id` and both device-id columns — see the issue reference chain). Nothing in the deployment can emit a composite or non-numeric id.\n\n## (b) The miss path is now Cache::flexible — no fake busy-503\n\nThe miss branch used to block on the upstream with no coordination. Both controllers now use:\n\n```php\nCache::flexible($cacheKey, [240, 300], fn () => ...compute from Zabbix...);\n```\n\n- A request arriving **while a refresh is in-flight** is served the stale value instead of erroring — no busy 503, no error-level log for mere contention (`Lock::get` is non-blocking; contention no longer qualifies as a service failure).\n- Widget UX effect: the widget may show data up to **5 minutes stale** (the staleness already accepted in the issue for both widgets) while the refresh happens out of band.\n- The refresh lock is released even when the upstream fails — no leaked locks, and the failed result is **never cached** (the compute throws, so flexible's write is skipped; recovery was proven in tests: throw → 503, then value → 200 with the upstream called twice total).\n- On the flexible TTL pair: the issue sanctions only **TTL 300** for both controllers. `240` is the fresh window inside that 300s total (values are fully fresh for 4 min, refresh-and-serve-stale for the last), chosen so refresh traffic cannot trip the Zabbix upstream rate limit. If the reviewer prefers a different fresh/total split, it is a one-line change in each controller.\n\n## (c) Tests updated for the numeric regex\n\n- `tests/Feature/MultiLatestValueControllerTest.php`: non-numeric fixtures (`item1`, `item2`, `item{n}`) replaced with numeric ids; new test `test_rejects_a_non_numeric_item_id_before_touching_the_upstream` (422 + upstream mock `->never()`); the 65-char length test now uses a *numeric* string so only `max:64` rejects it.\n- `tests/Feature/TrafficApiTest.php`: added non-numeric-id and 40-char-id 422 cases with `->never()` on the ZabbixService mock, a two-phase upstream-failure recovery test, a contention test (stale value served quietly, no error logs via `Log::spy()`), and an explicit frozen key-format assertion (`traffic_100_200_3600` / `multi_latest_<numeric ids>`).\n- `tests/Feature/MultiLatestValueApiTest.php`: tearDown-order fix only (its fixtures were already numeric).\n\n## Behavior notes for reviewers\n\n- The unchanged 503 contract is preserved by **throwing** from the flexible compute (`RuntimeException`) and letting the existing catch return the identical body `{'error':'Service temporarily unavailable'}`. The now-unreachable `unavailable()` helper was deleted from `TrafficController`; the error log now carries the exception text (side / failure kind / message).\n- Both Zabbix test files now run `parent::tearDown()` **before** `Mockery::close()` — with the old order, an unmet Mockery expectation skipped the RefreshDatabase rollback and stranded an open Postgres transaction that deadlocked the following test's setup.\n- `phpstan-baseline.neon` regenerated with the validation rewrite: **6 entries removed, 0 added**.\n- Untouched (per the issue scope): `SyncZabbixJob`, `ZabbixService`, the `zabbix_traffic_data` job cache, throttle limits, routes/token abilities, 503 response shape.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Scoped: 15 traffic + 12 multi-latest-controller + 5 multi-latest-api tests green (`32 passed, 0 failed`).\n- `vendor/bin/pint --dirty --test` clean; `composer phpstan` green after baseline regen (0 new entries).\n- Full suite via `composer test`: **2522 passed, 0 failed** (2 risky notes are pre-existing empty-selection tests in `HardwareIndexLivewireTest`, present before this branch).\n","headRefName":"perf/1019-constrain-zabbix-traffic-cache-key","title":"perf: constrain Zabbix item-id inputs and single-flight the cache miss (#1019)"}
